freopen with no name opens the stream's file again by /proc/self/fd/,
which lib/c has not: the stream keeps its descriptor, which takes the mode
as FreeBSD's freopen gives it. The access asked must be the descriptor's,
or it is open for both (EBADF otherwise, which POSIX lets freopen fail
with); O_APPEND is set or cleared, "w" truncates, "e" sets FD_CLOEXEC, and
the offset is the start but in append mode.

